<% content_for :title, "Privacy | ParkBack" %>

<section class="space-y-6 pb-6 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700">
  <div class="border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
    <h1 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">Privacy</h1>
  </div>

  <%= form_with url: privacy_preferences_path, method: :patch, data: { turbo: false }, class: "space-y-4 border-b border-slate-200 pb-6" do %>
    <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">Your choices</h2>
    <label class="flex items-start gap-3">
      <%= check_box_tag :analytics, "1", analytics_allowed?, class: "mt-1 size-4 shrink-0 accent-[#3a5f97]" %>
      <span><strong class="block text-ink">Optional analytics</strong>Off unless you choose it. Google Analytics uses cookies and receives visit information, including page URLs, device information, your IP address and a browser identifier. Parking data isn't included in analytics events.</span>
    </label>
    <label class="flex items-start gap-3">
      <%= check_box_tag :maps, "1", maps_allowed?, class: "mt-1 size-4 shrink-0 accent-[#3a5f97]" %>
      <span><strong class="block text-ink">Maps</strong>On by default. OpenStreetMap receives your IP address and the map area you're viewing. unpkg loads the map library and receives your IP address. Uncheck to turn maps off; GPS still works.</span>
    </label>
    <p>For saving, GPS starts with "Use my location". It also refreshes while you view or return to a saved spot, with your browser's permission. Maps don't enable analytics. These choices apply to newly loaded pages; reload other open tabs after changing them. Turning a service off doesn't erase information already sent.</p>
    <%= submit_tag "Save choices", class: "rounded-lg bg-navy px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-white" %>
  <% end %>

  <section class="space-y-3 border-b border-slate-200 pb-6">
    <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">Your parking data</h2>
    <%= link_to "Download my parking data", privacy_data_path, class: "inline-block text-navy underline", data: { turbo: false } %>
    <%= button_to "Delete my parking data", privacy_data_path, method: :delete,
          form: { data: { turbo: false } }, class: "rounded-lg border border-red-300 px-4 py-2 font-semibold text-red-700" %>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-2">
    <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">What we save</h2>
    <p>To help you find your vehicle, we save GPS coordinates and accuracy when available, the time, vehicle type, and any details or photo you add. Without GPS, a photo is required instead of a map pin. A signed cookie links the spot to this browser; no account is needed. Clearing cookies can break that link without deleting your saved data.</p>
    <p>Your walking location and compass readings are used in your browser for navigation, not saved to the parking database. Avoid sensitive details or other people's identifying information in notes or photos. Photos can include embedded location and camera details, which aren't removed.</p>
    <p>Separately from Google Analytics, we count daily and hourly page views to see how much ParkBack is used, without visitor identifiers or individual visit timestamps. This isn't a count of unique people. Reports cover 90 days; older totals are cleared when new views arrive.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="space-y-2">
    <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">Where it goes</h2>
    <p>Render hosts ParkBack and its server logs. Neon stores parking records and private photos in Singapore. The app checks your browser cookie before showing a photo; there's no public gallery. These services and the optional providers above may process information outside the Philippines. Operator access is limited to support, security and privacy requests.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="space-y-2">
    <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">When it's cleared</h2>
    <p>Found your vehicle? That button clears the spot and its photo, if any, from the app. "Delete my parking data" clears all spots linked to this browser. Otherwise, spots expire after seven days: access stops, and cleanup removes them on later requests, not necessarily at the exact expiry time.</p>
    <p>Neon may retain deleted photos in provider history or backups. Logs and optional analytics have separate retention rules, so deleting a spot doesn't erase every provider copy immediately. The parking cookie lasts up to seven days after use; your privacy choices are remembered for up to 180 days.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="space-y-2">
    <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">Questions or requests?</h2>
    <p>ParkBack is run by Lovely Joy Figueras. Email <%= mail_to "lovelyfigueras@gmail.com", "lovelyfigueras@gmail.com", class: "break-all text-navy underline" %> to ask about your data, get a copy, request a correction or deletion, object to its use, or make a complaint. Requests may need proof that the data is yours. You can also ask us to stop or limit how your data is used where applicable, change the choices above, or contact the <%= link_to "National Privacy Commission", "https://privacy.gov.ph/", class: "text-navy underline", rel: "noopener noreferrer" %>.</p>
  </section>

  <%= link_to "Back to ParkBack", root_path, class: "inline-block text-navy underline", data: { turbo: false } %>
</section>